  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through next Tuesday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Skies are mostly clear across much of\nnorthern and portions of central Nevada. Clouds and isolated light\nrain showers can be seen east of and including a Tonopah-Ruby \nLake-Montello line. This is due to an upper level trough currently\nspinning over southern California. This feature will take its \ntime moving east today. The light activity will come to an end \nlate this morning with skies becoming partly to mostly sunny due \nto slowly rising heights. Winds will be light in the north with \nbrisk conditions in the central as north to northwest winds 15 to \n25 mph with gusts to 35 mph will be felt. Highs today will be in \nthe 70s. Skies will be mostly clear tonight with lows in the 30s.\n\nBy Wednesday, the upper-level ridge off the West Coast will shift\ninland. This will bring a west to northwest flow aloft, bringing \nplentiful sunshine and dry conditions to all of northern and\ncentral Nevada. Temperatures will begin to rebound, with \nWednesday afternoon highs climbing back into the 70s and 80s with\novernight lows in the 30s and 40s. Winds will be light with\ngeneral afternoon breeziness to 20 mph.\n\nThe upper-level ridge remains the dominant weather \nfeature across the interior West on Thursday and lasting through\nthe early part of next week. This will keep the trend of dry, \nquiet, and pleasant fall weather lasting through the period. \nAfternoon highs will peak in the mid 70s to mid 80s, running above\nnormal for early October, while overnight lows comfortably settle\nin the 30s and 40s. A few locations could be near record high \ntemperatures by Friday or Saturday. \n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: Current forecast remains on\ntrack with only a few early morning adjustments made to the PoP\nand weather grids in central Nevada to account for the light\nshowers. Beyond the above mentioned timeframe, NBM forecast\nremains intact. Confidence is high in the dry weather and above\nnormal temperatures through the weekend.",
